India, Nepal, and the West. What are the 5 types of Tibetan music? Folk music dominates Tibetan music traditions with its variety, frequency, and emotional depth. Its five main types include song-and-dance, folk songs, work songs, storytelling songs, and instrumental music. Song-and-Dance Music: Known as the “ocean of song and dance,” Tibetan folk traditions blend singing and dancing seamlessly. How did Tibetan folk music evolve? During this period, a genre known as “Lu” emerged, setting the stage for the evolution of Tibetan musical traditions. These early compositions served as the foundation for the varied themes and styles that characterize Tibetan folk music today.",Lahta,Sino-Tibetan
