7,LHASSA STREET MUSICIANS TIBET CHINA | KINK GONG 2013 | kinkgong,https://kinkgong.bandcamp.com/album/lhassa-street-musicians-tibet-china,"August 21, 2021 - LHASSA STREET MUSICIANS TIBET CHINA JIA YANG PUBU 29 years old man from a village in Sajia, plays a ZHEMUNEI ( a 6 stringed plucked instrument) and NI MA 27 years old from a village in Dinri, sings. They usually perform in tea houses or places with tourists. 1 SONG OF THE VAGABOND, busking for money in winter in the streets of Lhassa, missing home 2 SONG ABOUT THEIR PARENTS, hoping to make money for them 3 SONG ABOUT TIBETAN PEOPLE being one family 4 CANG YANG JIA CUO love song RECORDED BY SHI TANDING JANUARY 2013",Lahta,Sino-Tibetan
8,Understanding the importance of Tibetan music,https://www.tibettravel.org/tibetan-culture/understanding-the-importance-of-tibetan-music.html,"May 6, 2025 - Songs celebrating Tibet’s traditions and past movements are commonplace for Tsering, and is well known and publicized for his fantastic, strong vocals; something which Tibetans believe is because of the high altitude. Some Tibetan singers have even made a name for themselves in neighbouring China and Japan including Alan Dowa Dolma and Gao Yuan Hong. Their voices are as powerful as Tsering’s, and fit the confines of Asian pop music extremely comfortably.",Lahta,Sino-Tibetan
9,Sino-Tibetan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/236/,"Lahta kvt, a language of Myanmar · Yinbaw kvu, a language of Myanmar · Yintale kvy, a language of Myanmar · Zayein kxk, a language of Myanmar · Peripheral 5 · Karen, Phrae Pwo kjt, a language of Thailand · Karen, Pwo Eastern kjp, a language of Myanmar ·",Lahta,Sino-Tibetan
